{"id": "EUVD-2026-80778", "enisaUuid": "4091a372-ae39-3885-a9bf-f4a728a17930", "description": "If a BIND resolver sends a query for a DNSSEC-signed authoritative zone, and the authoritative server replies with a valid wildcard answer and signed NSEC3 proof, followed by an unsigned NSEC at the same owner name, it will trigger an unexpected program exit.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T14:07:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T17:37:27", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-80274", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.29", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.26"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m66j-g9q7-jxjg", "CVE-2026-80274"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "21de2400-dd62-3bc1-a6f7-0354112a6144", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}, {"id": "42dc8e2c-5f1b-3c3b-93a7-3c3373a79695", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.25"}, {"id": "4c40621d-04ac-3f93-809f-37050b206953", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.27-S1"}, {"id": "8e7e6358-3306-3b35-ad1e-cf6b2aaf004f", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.27"}, {"id": "f8989f6d-b4d3-3d81-8d9b-54ba11ec150d", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.0 \u22649.18.50"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "43a51136-8eb5-3978-88c6-668294af22f0", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}